Question 25 (a): 

xy + \frac{1}{4} \pi x^2 = 36 

xy = 36 - \frac{1}{4} \pi x^2 \\ 
y = \frac{36}{x} - \frac{1}{4} \pi x \\ 

P = 2y + 2x + \frac{1}{4} \times 2 \pi x 

= 2 \left( \frac{36}{x} - \frac{1}{4} \pi x \right) + 2x + \frac{1}{2} \pi x 

= \frac{72}{x} - \frac{1}{2} \pi x + 2x + \frac{1}{2} \pi x 

= 2x + \frac{72}{x} 

Question 25 (b): 

\frac{dP}{dx} = 2 - \frac{72}{x^2} 

Setting \frac{dP}{dx} = 0, \text{ we have} 

2 = \frac{72}{x^2} \\ 
x^2 = 36 \\ 
x = 6 \quad (\text{since } x>0) 

\frac{d^2P}{dx^2} = \frac{144}{x^3} 

\text{When } x=6, 

\frac{d^2P}{dx^2} = \frac{144}{6^3} \text{ which is greater than zero.} 

\therefore \text{ P is a minimum when } x = 6. 

\text{The minimum perimeter } = 2 \times 6 + \frac{72}{6} 

= 12 + 12 

= 24 \text{ m}

